From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:29:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Make the default device before the frame locks the
 devices it draws with.

Making a Direct3D device takes a while: wined3d makes GL contexts and
probes the driver with them.  render_target() made the default device
under the locks of every device the frame draws with, so the
application's own drawing on those devices waited for it; Word's UI
thread sat in d2d_command_list_Close() behind the factory lock the
compositor held.  compositor_render() now makes the default device
before it takes any lock, when a target has neither a device of its
own nor one in its tree, and render_target() only takes a reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/compositor.c b/dlls/dcomp/compositor.c
index 1f0499a98bc..9f208fa285b 100644
--- a/dlls/dcomp/compositor.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/compositor.c
@@ -159,18 +159,30 @@ static HRESULT compositor_render( struct compositor *compositor, BOOL commit )
 {
     struct graphics_device **devices = NULL;
     unsigned int count = 0, size = 0, i;
+    BOOL need_default = FALSE;
     struct target *target;
+    ID3D11Device *d3d;
+    ID2D1Device *d2d;
     HRESULT hr = S_OK;
 
     compositor_lock( compositor );
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( target, &compositor->targets, struct target, entry )
     {
         if (!target->root) continue;
+        if (!target->device && !render_tree_device( target->root )) need_default = TRUE;
         if (FAILED(render_tree_devices( target->root, &devices, &count, &size ))) break;
     }
     for (i = 0; i < count; i++) ICompositionGraphicsDevice_AddRef( &devices[i]->ICompositionGraphicsDevice_iface );
     compositor_unlock( compositor );
 
+    /* A device of our own is made before any lock is taken: that takes a while, and the
+     * application draws with the devices locked below. */
+    if (need_default && SUCCEEDED(render_default_device( &d3d, &d2d )))
+    {
+        ID2D1Device_Release( d2d );
+        ID3D11Device_Release( d3d );
+    }
+
     for (i = 0; i < count; i++) graphics_device_lock( devices[i] );
     compositor_lock( compositor );
     if (commit)
